SECURITY HARDENING (Production-Level) — Implemented 2 May 2026
---------------------------------------------------------------
1. HTTP Security Headers via helmet
   - Content-Security-Policy (CSP)
   - X-Frame-Options: DENY
   - X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
   - Referrer-Policy: no-referrer
   - HSTS enabled in production
   - Permissions-Policy

2. CORS
   - Restricted via ALLOWED_ORIGINS env var (comma-separated list)
   - Permissive only in development (unset env var)

3. Request Body Limits
   - JSON and URL-encoded payloads capped at 512 KB (DoS prevention)

4. HTTP Parameter Pollution (hpp middleware)
   - Strips duplicate query parameters to prevent logic bypass attacks

5. Admin Endpoint Authentication — Bearer token (ADMIN_SECRET env var)
   The following endpoints require Authorization: Bearer <ADMIN_SECRET>:
   - POST   /api/articles              (create article)
   - PUT    /api/articles/:slug        (update article)
   - DELETE /api/articles/:slug        (delete article)
   - POST   /api/species               (create species)
   - PUT    /api/species/:slug         (update species)
   - DELETE /api/species/:slug         (delete species)
   - POST   /api/portfolio             (create portfolio clip)
   - DELETE /api/portfolio/:id         (delete portfolio clip)
   - GET    /api/contact/messages      (read inbox — contains PII)
   - PATCH  /api/contact/:id/read      (mark message read)
   - DELETE /api/contact/:id           (delete message)
   - GET    /api/newsletter            (list subscribers — contains PII)
   - GET    /api/analytics/summary     (analytics data)

   Public (no auth required):
   - GET  /api/articles, /api/articles/featured, /api/articles/stats
   - GET  /api/articles/:slug (also increments view count)
   - GET  /api/species, /api/species/:slug
   - GET  /api/portfolio, /api/categories, /api/tags, /api/feed.xml
   - POST /api/contact (submit contact form)
   - POST /api/newsletter (subscribe)
   - POST /api/newsletter/unsubscribe
   - POST /api/analytics/pageview

6. Input Sanitisation
   - validator.js escape(), normalizeEmail() on all user-submitted strings
   - Zod schema validation on all route bodies and query params

7. SQL Injection Prevention
   - All queries use Drizzle ORM parameterized statements
   - No raw SQL string interpolation anywhere

8. Production Error Handler
   - Stack traces suppressed in NODE_ENV=production
   - Generic "Internal server error" returned to client
   - Full error detail logged server-side via Pino

9. Graceful Shutdown
   - SIGTERM/SIGINT handlers close HTTP server then drain DB pool
   - 10-second forced exit fallback if shutdown hangs

10. Admin UI Auth Gate
    - /admin/messages requires secret key entry before any API call is made
    - Key is stored in localStorage; "Lock" button clears it immediately
    - All fetch calls include Authorization: Bearer <secret>
    - 401 response automatically re-shows the lock screen


ENVIRONMENT VARIABLES
---------------------
Variable          Required  Description
DATABASE_URL      YES       PostgreSQL connection string (auto-provisioned on Replit)
PORT              YES       API server port (auto-set by Replit to 8080)
ADMIN_SECRET      YES       Bearer token for all admin/write endpoints — set in Replit Secrets
ALLOWED_ORIGINS   No        Comma-separated allowed CORS origins (permissive if unset)
VITE_SENTRY_DSN   No        Sentry project DSN — error tracking disabled if unset


